Based on my research, I found that the --n-cpu-moe flag in llama.cpp refers to --spec-draft-n-cpu-moe which specifies how many layers of Mixture of Experts (MoE) weights should be kept in CPU memory for the draft model during speculative decoding. This allows partial offloading of MoE weights to CPU to improve performance or compatibility when running large language models with expert layers.

